  "requirement": "A `{req}` definition MUST use an opening fence of at least three colons immediately followed by `{req} <name>`. A closing fence MUST have at least as many colons as the opening fence. The requirement body MUST be all Markdown between those fence lines, including headings, examples, diagrams, and blank lines, and MUST NOT include text after the closing fence. Leading and trailing whitespace MUST be excluded when comparing the body with evidence.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: the requirement is met.** The implementation matches each clause of `requirements.ci.span`, and the tests cover the main cases. A few edge cases have no dedicated test.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `definition_blocks` in `src/lib.rs` finds opening fences with `colon_fence`. That helper accepts at most 3 leading spaces and requires at least 3 colons.\n- It then requires the text after the colons to start with `{req}`, `{example}` or `{definition}`. After that it requires whitespace and a valid name, so `{req} <name>` follows the fence immediately.\n- The closing fence is the first later line that meets three conditions:\n  - it is a colon fence,\n  - it has at least as many colons as the opening fence,\n  - nothing follows the colons except whitespace.\n\n  Lines inside Markdown code blocks (found with pulldown-cmark offsets) are skipped. A `:::` line inside a code block therefore cannot end the requirement early.\n- The body is `body_start..body_end`, which is everything between the fence lines. This includes headings, setext headings, code blocks, blank lines and nested shorter directives. A closing line with trailing text is not accepted as a closer, so text after the closing fence is never part of the body.\n- In `collect_definitions` in `src/evidence.rs` (marked `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.span`), the body is taken as `content[block.body_start..block.body_end].trim()`. This excludes leading and trailing whitespace.\n- An unclosed fence is reported as an error. The evidence text check (`requirements.ci.requirement_text`) compares the evidence string with this trimmed body.\n\n**Tests**\n- `colon_requirement_span_includes_markdown_and_excludes_following_text` (`src/evidence.rs`) uses a body containing:\n  - a code block holding `:::`,\n  - an ATX heading,\n  - a setext heading,\n  - blank lines.\n\n  A following paragraph and a second requirement must be excluded. The evidence text contains no surrounding newlines, so the whitespace trimming is exercised implicitly.\n- `reports_a_missing_closing_colon_fence` (`src/evidence.rs`) checks that an unclosed block is reported.\n- `a_longer_colon_fence_contains_a_shorter_nested_directive` (`src/lib.rs`) uses a four-colon opening with a nested three-colon directive. It asserts the exact body range, that the block is closed, and that the following text is outside the block.\n\n**Minor gaps**\nThere is no dedicated test for a closing fence that has trailing text, or for a closing fence with too few colons. The code handles both correctly. These do not block a true determination, and there are no FIXME markers.",
